DOM order: energy, hand, end-turn. To give hand full width on mobile, set `.hand-bar { flex-wrap: wrap; }` with `.hand-scroll { order: -1; flex-basis: 100%; }` and then energy/endturn on second row. But end-turn's turn indicator would be below. Could use `display:grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; grid-template-areas: "hand hand hand" "energy . end"` with hand spanning. But the turn indicator inside end-turn-wrap would be in second row. Height increases by card height (~116px) + 48 = 164 vs current ~116. Adds 48px. On 844 height fine; on 640 height maybe board needs scroll, but battle-main can scroll. Could be acceptable. However on mobile the hand is key; full width shows 4 of 5 cards (86px * 4 + gaps = 362) within 378. Good.

But maybe better use smaller cards and keep one row, with a fade/peek indicator. The current UX of 2 cards visible is poor. Let's implement two-row footer on mobile <=560px, but ensure it doesn't consume too much vertical space. We can set hand card width 78px; full width 378 -> 4.7 cards, so 4 visible. Hand height ~118. Footer total ~170. Board area: 844 - topbar 56 - enemy banner 50 - footer 170 = 568, enough for 6 rows * 46 = 276 plus log. On 640 height: 640-56-50-170=364, board scroll. Fine.

Alternatively, make hand cards smaller 72px and keep single row with hand full width by putting controls in a floating overlay? Hmm.

Let's test two-row layout via CSS only at max-width 560. Add:
```
.hand-bar { flex-wrap: wrap; }
.hand-scroll { order: -1; flex: 1 0 100%; padding-bottom: 0; }
.energy-orb { order: 0; }
.end-turn-wrap { order: 1; margin-left: auto; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
.end-turn-btn { min-width: 92px; }
.turn-indicator { font-size: 7.5px; }
```
Actually with flex-wrap and hand order -1 full basis, energy/end-turn second row. End-turn wrap includes button + turn indicator; set flex-direction row to save vertical. `.end-turn-wrap` currently column. On mobile row: button then indicator. Could make indicator text beside. Height 48. Fine.

But note `.hand-scroll .game-card` height is determined by card face aspect ratio; 86px width gives ~118 height. Footer 6+118+48+8 =180. Screenshot hand area currently starts at y=664 and card bottom 780; footer bottom 844; with new layout cards start 620? Actually footer grows upward, battle-main shrinks. Good.

Could also hide card text on mobile hand to reduce card height, but then stats/name still? The card face has name, type, text, stats. Hiding `.card-text` makes cards shorter (~80px) and still playable. On mobile, users can tap to select and see description in logline. Maybe best: hide card text in hand at <=560 to make cards compact, but then they can't compare effects. The hand card could retain stats and name. The logline shows selected card description ("Lanciere · Perfora..."). That is a good UX. But the cards currently show text at 7px, cramped. Hiding text would improve visibility and height. Yet the screenshot shows card text at 7px unreadable. So hide text on mobile hand, show art, name, type, stats; selected card description appears above. That also shrinks card height. Let's inspect card CSS.

