Let's implement full-width hand row on mobile only. This improves access. Also maybe reduce card width to 80 to show 4.5. Let's do:

```
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .hand-bar { flex-wrap: wrap; row-gap: 4px; }
  .hand-scroll { order: -1; flex: 1 0 100%; padding-top: 1px; }
  .hand-scroll .game-card { flex-basis: 74px; width: 74px; }
  .energy-orb { width: 42px; height: 42px; }
  .energy-orb .e-val { font-size: 15px; }
  .energy-orb .e-label { font-size: 5.5px; }
  .end-turn-wrap { flex: 1; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 8px; }
  .end-turn-btn { min-height: 42px; min-width: 96px; }
}
```

But `.end-turn-wrap` order default 0; energy default order 0 before hand? hand order -1 ensures first visual row. With wrap, hand takes 100%, then energy and end-turn on second row. End-turn flex:1 with row direction; indicator inside should be left of button or after? DOM: button then indicator. With justify-content flex-end, they'll be at right; energy left, gap. Good. Turn indicator may be too long; but fine.

However energy orb and end-turn row: energy at left, end-turn row at right; gap between. Fine. Footer height: hand 126 + 42 + paddings ~180. On 844: board area ~844-56-50-180=558, enough. On 640: ~354, board scroll. But this makes hand cards 74px wide; 5 cards*74+gaps=394 > 378, 4.8 visible; great.

Let's implement. Ensure desktop unchanged.

